    question: 'Can I make money selling online courses?',
    answer: '<p>Yep. Online courses are one of the most profitable digital products. Global e-learning market exceeds three hundred billion and continues growing ten to fifteen percent annually.</p><p>Realistic expectations:</p><p>First course one thousand to ten thousand with proper marketing.<br/>Established creators ten thousand to one hundred thousand annually.<br/>Top creators one million plus annually.</p><p>Success depends more on your audience and marketing than the platform you choose. Build an email list validate your course idea and price based on value delivered.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Udemy or my own platform?',
    answer: '<p>Use Udemy if you have no existing audience want marketplace discovery and are okay with lower per-sale revenue. Udemy\'s fifty-seven million students can discover your course but you keep only thirty-seven percent of sales they generate.</p><p>Use your own platform if you have an audience like email list or social following want to build a brand and keep more revenue. Platforms like Teachable let you keep ninety-five to one hundred percent of sales.</p><p>Many creators do both. Use Udemy for discovery and their own platform for premium courses with higher prices.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Equipment needed to create an online course?',
    answer: '<p>Minimum setup under one hundred bucks:</p><p>Your smartphone since modern phones shoot excellent video.<br/>Natural lighting or a thirty dollar ring light.<br/>A quiet room.<br/>Free screen recording like OBS or Loom free tier.</p><p>Professional setup five hundred to fifteen hundred:</p><p>USB microphone Blue Yeti or Rode NT-USB one hundred to one seventy.<br/>Webcam Logitech C nine twenty or C nine twenty-two seventy to one hundred.<br/>Lighting Elgato Key Light or softbox kit one hundred to two hundred.<br/>Screen recording Camtasia or ScreenFlow two fifty to three hundred.</p><p>Audio quality matters more than video quality. Invest in a good microphone first.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'How long should an online course be?',
    answer: '<p>Course length depends on the topic and price point:</p><p>Mini-course twenty to fifty bucks runs thirty to sixty minutes.<br/>Standard course one hundred to three hundred runs two to five hours.<br/>Premium course five hundred plus runs five to twenty plus hours.</p><p>Focus on outcomes not duration. A two-hour course that delivers results is more valuable than a twenty-hour course with padding. Students want transformation not content for content\'s sake.</p><p>Break content into five to fifteen minute lessons for better engagement and completion rates.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Need a website to sell courses?',
    answer: '<p>Nope. Platforms like Teachable Kajabi and Thinkific host your course pages sales pages and checkout. You can launch with just the platform.</p><p>However having your own website helps with:</p><p>SEO and organic traffic.<br/>Building authority and trust.<br/>Email list building.<br/>Content marketing like blog or podcast.</p><p>Start with just the course platform then add a website as you grow and want more control over your brand.</p>'
  }
